178	<h2>Proposed changes</h2>
179	<p>These four changes come from the review of the process&rsquo;s dead ends of 23 November 2026. Each waits for the curator&rsquo;s yes to its exact words. A comment on an item, or a word in chat, answers it.</p>
180	
181	<section id="g1" class="part group">
182	<h3><span class="num">Drafts 43 to 65 &middot; 23 passages of SKILL.md and the parts record.md, delegating.md, road.md and batch.md</span>The review queue holds only questions</h3>
183	<p class="outcome"><strong>For the curator.</strong> A decision that a batch landed and that is not consequential no longer waits for the curator&rsquo;s review. One short report for each landing tells the curator what changed, and the queue holds only questions.</p>
184	<section id="d43" class="part item">
185	<h4><span class="num">Draft 43 &middot; SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;review queue&rdquo;, line 28</span>The review queue holds only questions</h4>
186	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Proposed text, not landed; underlined, the words that come in.</span>
187	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;review queue&rdquo;, line 28</p>
188	<dl class="gloss"><dt>review queue</dt><dd><code>explorations/coordinator/review-queue.md</code>, the one home of each <span class="add">question</span> that waits for the curator's <span class="add">word,</span> numbered and sorted by theme. <span class="add">A question is a consequential decision, a re-approval row that the work has reached, or a landed decision that the curator objected to.</span> A pointer cites an item by its number.</dd></dl>
189	</div></div>
190	<details class="prior"><summary>Current text (tap to open)</summary><div>
191	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;review queue&rdquo;, line 28</p>
192	<dl class="gloss"><dt>review queue</dt><dd><code>explorations/coordinator/review-queue.md</code>, the one home of each <span class="cut">item</span> that waits for the curator's <span class="cut">word or review,</span> numbered and sorted by theme. A pointer cites an item by its number.</dd></dl>
193	</div></details>
194	<div class="note"><p><strong>What it changes, and why.</strong> The queue held every landed default for a later review, so it grew faster than the curator could read it. Now it holds only questions, and the definition says which things are questions. The change gives up the queue as a list of everything that landed.</p></div>
195	</section>
196	<section id="d44" class="part item">
197	<h4><span class="num">Draft 44 &middot; SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 31</span>A landed default is named in the landing report, not queued</h4>
198	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Proposed text, not landed; underlined, the words that come in.</span>
199	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 31</p>
200	<dl class="gloss"><dt>default</dt><dd>Option that stands unless the curator picks another: the one that an ask recommends, or the choice that an agent landed without the curator's word, which FACTS states and <span class="add">the landing report names or counts.</span></dd></dl>
